|Your first ML model in Python|

We will use Linear Regression to predict a house price from its size.

Install: pip install scikit-learn

from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression

# X = input feature: house size in square feet
X = [[500], [700], [1000], [1200], [1500]]    ----> historical data

# y = known house prices in lakhs
y = [20, 28, 40, 48, 60]     ------------------> known outcomes

# Create the model
model = LinearRegression()   -----> model, creates algorithm 

# Train the model
model.fit(X, y)   -------> training a model 

# Predict the price of a 900 sq. ft. house
prediction = model.predict([[900]])     --------> prediction using the trained model 

print(prediction[0])
-------------------------------------------------------------
Features (X) — Input variables given to the model.
Target variable / Label (y) — The output the model learns to predict.
LinearRegression()  --Creates the algorithm
model.fit(X, y) --Trains the model
model.predict([[900]]) --Predicts the price for new input
